NBIS (NIST Biometric Image Software) - vendored subset
=======================================================

What this is
-------------
Just the two libraries fingerprint_server needs for real minutiae-based
matching (replacing the earlier placeholder correlation matcher):

  mindtct/  - minutiae extraction from a raw 8-bit grayscale fingerprint
              image (entry point: get_minutiae(), mindtct/getmin.c)
  bozorth3/ - minutiae-set matching, producing an integer match score
              (entry points: bozorth_probe_init()/bozorth_to_gallery(),
              bozorth3/bz_drvrs.c)

Both are U.S. government work, public domain (see the license header at
the top of every vendored .c/.h file) - no licensing restriction on use,
modification, or redistribution.

Where this came from
----------------------
Pristine upstream NBIS source, as mirrored at
https://github.com/lessandro/nbis (a straight mirror of NIST's own NBIS
distribution - not libfprint's copy, which has been modified to depend on
GLib allocators and libfprint's own GObject-based minutiae/print data
model via a replaced fpi-minutiae.h; this vendored copy intentionally
avoids both of those couplings and is plain, dependency-free ANSI C).

Exact source paths pulled from that mirror:
  mindtct/src/lib/mindtct/*.c   -> mindtct/
  mindtct/include/{lfs,log,morph,mytime}.h -> include/
  bozorth3/src/lib/bozorth3/*.c -> bozorth3/
  bozorth3/include/{bozorth,bz_array}.h    -> include/
  commonnbis/include/{defs,usebsd}.h       -> include/

What was deliberately NOT vendored
------------------------------------
mindtct's isempty.c, mytime.c, results.c, to_type9.c, update.c, and the
bozorth3 CLI binary's own main() (a different file at
bozorth3/src/bin/bozorth3/bozorth3.c upstream, not the same-named library
file under src/lib/ that *is* vendored here) - none of these are needed
to call get_minutiae()/bozorth_to_gallery() from fingerprint_server.

Patches applied (in include/lfs.h and include/log.h, see the files
themselves for the exact diffs - intentionally kept as small, in-place
edits rather than separate .patch files, since there are only a few)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. lfs.h: removed `#include <an2k.h>` - that header (and the RECORD/
   FIELD/ANSI_NIST types it provides) is only needed by
   to_type9.c/update.c, which aren't vendored here. Their extern
   declarations in lfs.h were removed too (they'd fail to compile
   without an2k.h's types).
2. lfs.h: added `#include <stdlib.h>` and `#include <string.h>` -
   needed for malloc/free/realloc/memcpy/memset, which several mindtct
   files call without including them directly (relying on an implicit
   declaration, which newer GCC treats as an error/warning depending on
   the function).
3. log.h: added `#include <string.h>` for the same reason as #2 - a
   couple of mindtct files only include log.h, not lfs.h.

No other files were modified. Compiles cleanly as plain C (gcc -Wall)
with these two patches - the only warnings are a handful of
unused-variable/misleading-indentation notices in upstream code,
suppressed via SubDirCcFlags in the Jamfile rather than touched here.

Updating this vendored copy later
------------------------------------
Re-fetch the same file list from the same mirror (or any pristine NBIS
source - this is not libfprint-specific), then re-apply the two lfs.h
patches above by hand (they're small and self-explanatory in context).
